  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1\\,=\\,2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+1 \\\\  & {x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+0x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+8x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+7x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $2x+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $3{x}^{2}+7x+5.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+1}{\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4\\,} & =2x+1+\\frac{3{x}^{2}+7x+5}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
